    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="0558" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg524"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 735.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copies
                    and translations of two notes recently received from the Spanish Government
                    relative to the case of Manuel Fernandez Chaquielo. In this connection, and
                    referring to your No. 729, of the 14th ultimo, I beg to call the Department’s
                    attention to the fact that the only information I have ever received regarding
                    the murder of Govin has been that contained in the Department’s telegrams and
                    despatches upon the Chaquielo case; and that, consequently, I have never been
                    able to make a formal presentation of that (Govin’s) case to the Spanish
                    Government.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d554-a1.xml" xpointer="d554-a1"/>
